From e600fcd78f3151a80d3c67385a738b641bec4102 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 15:21:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] version: bump EXTENDNO to Reaper_v2.3.4

v2.3.3 was built and flashed on the RT-BE96U before the framed-overlay
regression above (1d9d58a2be) was found, so the fix ships as its own version
rather than changing what v2.3.3 means. Two different images must never share a
version string - that is exactly what the CI EXPECTED_VERSION assertion exists
to catch, and the tested-tonight image is v2.3.3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src-rt/version.conf | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src-rt/version.conf b/release/src-rt/version.conf
index 5edc884552..fb690bee83 100644
--- a/release/src-rt/version.conf
+++ b/release/src-rt/version.conf
@@ -4,6 +4,6 @@ KERNEL_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(KERNEL_VER))
 FS_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(FS_VER))
 
 SERIALNO=102.8
-EXTENDNO=Reaper_v2.3.3
+EXTENDNO=Reaper_v2.3.4
 
 RCNO=0
-- 
2.25.1

